Description: the %cd actions of mc.ext.ini (archives: tar, zip, 7z, rar, ISO...) copied the path into a static buffer of 1 KB without a bound: a GString instead
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/694c66817ae106e3cadf8f3c22e9fea6530df93b
 (22.03.2026, after 4.8.33; no release has it), backported to the code of 4.8.33
 (its text is a char * there, not a GString)
Bug: https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/issues/5115
Why: a buffer overflow by the contents of an archive. Enter on a file whose name is
 longer than 1 KB (a tar entry can have such a name: pax, GNU long names) with an
 action "%cd %p/<vfs>://" (ours: ubsdtar, utar...) wrote past the static buffer of
 src/filemanager/ext.c with strcpy(): mc 4.8.33 crashed (tools/mc-test.sh opens such
 a tar). The command for %cd is built in a GString of exec_extension() now, freed at
 its end.

